Nabu Linux hardware support includes work derived from the Nabu Fedora
configuration packages published at:

    https://github.com/jhuang6451/nabu_fedora_packages

The ALSA UCM profile retains its original author attribution to map220v and was
distributed as part of the MIT-licensed nabu-fedora-configs-core package. Local
changes add conservative direct-ASP speaker settings and four-channel playback
metadata for ongoing Linux hardware validation.

The Plasma output profiles and Nabu boot integration files were validated and
adapted for this project. Generated identifiers in the profile examples are
not credentials.

